ealth Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-de7597f6d5e0","stem":"which will also identify the supervisors of the","type":"Image / Diagram Question","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"review","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","requires_visual_review"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":true,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["prior_structural_review_flag","requires_visual_review","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic","visual_asset_not_transcribed"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5513731b0903","stem":"which are publishable in a peer reviewed Journal. The","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-72f555029c66","stem":"During an autopsy a parenchymal fatty dystrophy of the myocardium was diag- nosed. What is the common or descriptive name of the heart due to this dystrophy?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*‘Tabby cat‘ heart ( ̳Tiger‘s‘ heart)"},{"label":"B","text":"Bovine heart"},{"label":"C","text":"̳Hairy‘ heart"},{"label":"D","text":"Solder plaque (bony heart)"},{"label":"E","text":"Cor pulmonale"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-a38128841b22","stem":"A patient with leukemia died from severe chronic anemia. An autopsy revealed an enlarged heart, with flabby myocardium. It had a dim pale-grey color, yellow spots and bars. Which pathological process was found in the heart at post-mortem?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Parenchymal fatty dystrophy"},{"label":"B","text":"Vacuolar dystrophy."},{"label":"C","text":"Hydropic dystrophy."},{"label":"D","text":"Mesenchymal fatty dystrophy."},{"label":"E","text":"Mixed dystrophy."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-57689942f6f2","stem":"A 53 year old patient died with symptoms of liver insufficiency. A post-mortem examination revealed the enlarged, flabby, yellow-brown liver. Gross examination of the liver‘s section showed drops of fat. Microscopically: hepatocytes on the pe- ripheries of the hepatic lobules contained masses of small drops within the cytop- lasm. Which process most likely took place in the liver?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Fatty dystrophy of the liver"},{"label":"B","text":"Glucosylceramide lipidosis (Gaucher‘s disease)"},{"label":"C","text":"Sphingolopidosis (Niemann-Pick disease)"},{"label":"D","text":"Gangliosidosis (Тay-Sachs disease)"},{"label":"E","text":"Systemic lipoidoses"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7c45b0cd0b6f","stem":"A patient died from chronic cardiovascular insufficiency. At the post-mortem a ‘tabby cat‘ heart was found. From the side of the endocardium, a yellow-white striped pattern was noticeable. The myocardium was a dim with gray-yellow color. Which process is most likely diagnosed?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Fatty parenchymal dystrophy."},{"label":"B","text":"Carbohydrate dystrophy"},{"label":"C","text":"Hydropic dystrophy."},{"label":"D","text":"Fatty mesenchymal dystrophy."},{"label":"E","text":"Amyloidosis."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e455869003d1","stem":"A seven-year-old child presented with diphtheria of the pharynx. He subsequent- ly died from acute cardiac insufficiency. Post-mortem examination of the heart revealed that the cavities of the heart were extended horizontally. Muscle of the heart were dim and flabby. Gross section showed motley appearance, with yellow areas. Microscopically in the cytoplasm of some myocardial cells small vacuoles were determined. The frozen sections showed vacuoles within cells stained with sudan-III in orange color. Which type of dystrophy was found in myocardial cells?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Fatty dystrophy 3"},{"label":"B","text":"Carbohydrate dystrophy"},{"label":"C","text":"Vacuolar dystrophy"},{"label":"D","text":"Hyaline dystrophy"},{"label":"E","text":"Hydropic dystrophy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-1f370c5a5425","stem":"A man died due to cardiac insufficiency. At autopsy revealed the heart increased volume and flabby. A myocardium was a clay-yellow color and dim. From the side of the endocardium a yellow-white striped pattern was visible ( ̳tabby cat‘). Under the microscope the groups of myocardial cells lost their normal structure, their cy- toplasm contained shallow drops which were black when stained with sudan-IV. Which one of the following is the correct diagnosis?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Fatty dystrophy of myocardium"},{"label":"B","text":"Cardiosclerosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Rheumatic myocarditis"},{"label":"D","text":"Obesity of the heart"},{"label":"E","text":"Myomalacia"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-e55cdffbeb58","stem":"A 66-year-old male died from cardiac insufficiency. During the dissection an increase volume heart was found. Observation of the heart revealed a flabby consis- tency with stretched chambers. The myocardium section had a dim, clay-yellowish color. From the side of the endocardium a yellow-white striped pattern was present, which was especially noted in the papillary muscles. Which pathological process is the most credible?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Fatty dystrophy of the myocardium"},{"label":"B","text":"Obesity of the heart"},{"label":"C","text":"Dilatation cardiomyopathy"},{"label":"D","text":"Myomalacia"},{"label":"E","text":"Cardiosclerosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a1b1d83ad77a","stem":"A patient died from pulmonary-cardiac insufficiency. During the dissection a significantly enlarged anemic liver, with yellow doughy consistencies was found. A liver specimen stained with hematoxylin and eosin exposed various sizes of va- cuoles in the cytoplasm of the hepatocytes. Which one of the following dystrophies occurred?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Parenchymal fatty"},{"label":"B","text":"Parenchymal carbohydrate"},{"label":"C","text":"Hyaline"},{"label":"D","text":"Mesenchymal fatty"},{"label":"E","text":"Hydropic"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-adb3f931fcc1","stem":"A 38-year-old patient, suffering from chronic alcoholism and cirrhosis of the liver, developed profuse bleeding due to varicose veins of the esophagus which resulted in death. During the autopsy a liver was noted to be diminished in size with micronodular tuberosity. The organ was dense and rather yellow in color. A histological evaluation of the cryostat specimens of the liver, stained with hema- toxylin and eosin, revealed hepatocytes with large, optically empty vacuoles. These vacuoles were black when stained with osmium acid. These optically empty va- 4 cuoles hepatocytes indicate","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Fatty dystrophy"},{"label":"B","text":"Inclusions of hyaline."},{"label":"C","text":"Alcoholic hyaline (Mallory bodies)"},{"label":"D","text":"Vacuolar dystrophy."},{"label":"E","text":"Carbohydrates dystrophy."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-de71a6190681","stem":"A 16-year-old girl presents with the symptoms of sharp pain during swallow- ing, lymph node enlargement of the neck, and the body temperature of 38°C. The mucous membrane of the tonsils revealed grayish membranes with yellow tapes with were not easily separated from the defect. The patient‘s state progressively worsened which death occurring on the 8th day of the disease due to cardiac insuf- ficiency. Which of following histological changes in the myocardial cells will be the most likely finding?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Fatty dystrophy"},{"label":"B","text":"Hydropic dystrophy"},{"label":"C","text":"Hyaline dystrophy"},{"label":"D","text":"Ballooning dystrophy"},{"label":"E","text":"Mucous dystrophy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8aaa8634ebb3","stem":"A 44-year-old woman died from chronic alcoholic intoxication. During the au- topsy a significantly enlarged liver of doughy consistency and rather yellowish color was found. Microscopically, after staining with hematoxylin and eosin, cytop- lasm of the hepatocytes contained optically empty vacuoles. Which type of dystro- phy has taken place?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Parenchymal fatty dystrophy"},{"label":"B","text":"Carbohydrate parenchymal dystrophy"},{"label":"C","text":"Hyaline dystrophy"},{"label":"D","text":"Mesenchymal fatty dystrophy"},{"label":"E","text":"Hydropic dystrophy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b4d124b67fd8","stem":"A patient has died from toxic sepsis. During dissection a ̳tabby cat‘ ( ̳tiger‘s heart‘) was found. Microscopically, lipids were detected in the cytoplasm of the myocardial cells. What is the primary morphological mechanism for development for this dystrophy?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Medical Biochemistry","topic":"Lipids","topicOriginal":"Lipids","subtopic":"Lipid","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Decomposition"},{"label":"B","text":"Infiltration"},{"label":"C","text":"Transformation"},{"label":"D","text":"Pathological synthesis."},{"label":"E","text":"Neoplastic alterations."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Medical Biochemistry","displayTopic":"Lipids","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-407ed745a05c","stem":"Ultrastructural investigation of a liver biopsy, revealed that between the mito- chondria there were numerous flat cisterns and bubbles with secretory granules circumscribed with membrane. Name a cell structure with the hyperplasic constitu- ents?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Golgi apparatus"},{"label":"B","text":"Pinocytosis bubbles 5"},{"label":"C","text":"Endoplasmic reticulum"},{"label":"D","text":"Lysosoms"},{"label":"E","text":"Microtubes"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","subject_suggestion_available"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_suggestion_available","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-7fe52699e601","stem":"A 42-year-old female became ill with diphtheria and died from acute cardiac insufficiency. During dissection it was noted that the heart cavities were extended and that the muscle of the heart was dim, motley and on a cut surface had yellow areas. Which process was exposed in the myocardial cells?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Fatty dystrophy"},{"label":"B","text":"Carbohydrate dystrophy"},{"label":"C","text":"Ballooning dystrophy"},{"label":"D","text":"Hyaline dystrophy"},{"label":"E","text":"Hydropic dystrophy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e1ae13478512","stem":"During the examination of a newborn, some apparent skin differences are noted. The skin is dry, with an uneven surface and with the presence of grey plates which can be removed layer by layer. These changes are related to which type of dystrophy?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Horny dystrophy"},{"label":"B","text":"Hydropic dystrophy"},{"label":"C","text":"Hyaline dystrophy"},{"label":"D","text":"Fibrinoid swelling"},{"label":"E","text":"Mucoid swelling"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bc2cba15e82e","stem":"A male patient had a prosthetic appliance on the lower jaw. The ventral surface of tongue revealed a dense, gray plaque with a clear boundary. Histology revealed the thickened of the stratified squamous epithelium due granular and to basal layers thickening, hyperkeratosis, acanthosis, lymphocyte‘s infiltration of connective tis- sue. Make a diagnosis.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Leukoplakia"},{"label":"B","text":"Erythroplakia"},{"label":"C","text":"Papilloma"},{"label":"D","text":"Cancer in sity (intra-epithelial neoplasia)"},{"label":"E","text":"Condyloma"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8370e1a0b212","stem":"During the preventive examination of a worker employed in the coal resins production the areas of thickening and keratinization of the mucous membrane in the oral cavity were found. This occured mainly on the cheeks areas, showing a whitish color with a rough surface. They were not painful. Which pathology is this related to?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Leukoplakia"},{"label":"B","text":"Papillomatosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Glossitis"},{"label":"D","text":"Stomatitis"},{"label":"E","text":"Calcification"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b5da990ef28c","stem":"A 45-year old male is found to have a severe intoxication. A diagnosis of sepsis is made. Several days later he dies. At autopsy, his myocardium grossly had a ̳tiger 6 heart‘ pattern. . Microscopically, lipids were detected in the cytoplasm of cardiac hystiocytes. What morphogenetic mechanism prevails in the development of this dystrophy?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Decomposition.."},{"label":"B","text":"Infiltration."},{"label":"C","text":"Transformation"},{"label":"D","text":"Abnormal synthesis."},{"label":"E","text":"Colliquation."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-8516f7464263","stem":"A 3-month- old infant dies and autopsy is requested. Electron microscopic ex- amination of liver tissue revealed a great amount of flat cisterns and vesicles with secretory granules, surrounded by membrane, scattered among numerous mito- chondria. Which of the following cell ultra structures has been shown to be hyper- plastic?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Golgi complex."},{"label":"B","text":"Pinocytic vesicles."},{"label":"C","text":"Endoplasmic reticulum."},{"label":"D","text":"Lysosomes."},{"label":"E","text":"Filaments."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d3a6682c2204","stem":"A 36-year-old female develops liver failure followed with lethal outcome. Au- topsy has shown an enlarged liver of yellow-brown color and soft consistence. Drops of fat are noticed on the liver cut surface and on the scalpel. Microscopical- ly: hepatocytes at peripheral zone of a liver lobules contain small drops that fill cytoplasm and push the nucleus to the periphery. What process in the liver do the following changes testify to?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Fatty degeneration of liver."},{"label":"B","text":"Cerebrosidelipidosis (Gaucher's disease)."},{"label":"C","text":"Sphingomyelinlipidosis (Niemann — Pick disease)."},{"label":"D","text":"Gangliosidelipidosis (Tay —Sachs disease)."},{"label":"E","text":"Generalized gangliosidosis (Norman—Landing disease)."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-69b2efb1101f","stem":"Autopsy of a menopausal woman with a ling history of a chronic ischemic heart disease revealed soft and enlarged heart. Its chambers were extended; the myocar- dium sectional view was lack-luster with grey- yellowish coloring. An endocar- dium presented with yellow-white banding, most evident in papillary muscles. What is the most likely pathological process in woman‘s heart?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Fatty degeneration of myocardium."},{"label":"B","text":"Fatty heart."},{"label":"C","text":"Dilated cardiomyopathy."},{"label":"D","text":"Myomalation."},{"label":"E","text":"Cardiosclerosis."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6e862028da05","stem":"A 77-year-old male with a dental prosthesis on his upper jaw is seen by his dentist because of a solid gray patch on his tongue. A lesion has irregular contour, uneven surface, and clear borders. Microscopic investigation of its biopsy revealed the thickening of stratified squamous epithelium, its hyperkeratosis, and acanthosis 7 accompanied with lymphocytes and macrophages infiltration of subjacent connec- tive tissue. What is the most likely diagnosis?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Leukoplakia."},{"label":"B","text":"Erythroplakia."},{"label":"C","text":"Papilloma."},{"label":"D","text":"Cancer in situ."},{"label":"E","text":"Condyloma."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-b0f08e368a3b","stem":"An autopsy of a patient, who died of progressive anemia due to leukemia, re- vealed enlarged and flabby heart. The cut surface the myocardium was dim, pale- gray with subendocardial yellow spots and streaks. Which of the following patho- logic processes had developed in the heart?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Parenchymal fatty dystrophy."},{"label":"B","text":"Vacuolar dystrophy."},{"label":"C","text":"Hyaline-drop dystrophy."},{"label":"D","text":"Mesenchymal fatty dystrophy."},{"label":"E","text":"Workload hypertrophy Connective tissue’s (mesenchymal) dystrophy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f9115a971cb7","stem":"A 56 year old female has been ill with chronic fibrocavernous tuberculosis of the lungs for the past 20 years. She entered the nephrology department with an uremia syndrome. A test for the presence of amyloid in kidneys was positive. Which form of amyloid is indicated in this case?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Secondary"},{"label":"B","text":"Primary"},{"label":"C","text":"Localized"},{"label":"D","text":"Familial congenital"},{"label":"E","text":"Senile"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-55509f1c8acd","stem":"The dissection of a 49 year old male reveals a deformed mitral valve, which is thickened and does not completely close. Microscopically the foci of the collagen fibers are eosinophilic and give a positive reaction on a fibrin test? The most credi- ble explanation is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Fibrinoid swelling"},{"label":"B","text":"Fibrinoid inflammation"},{"label":"C","text":"Mucoid swelling"},{"label":"D","text":"Hyalinosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Amyloidosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a9c092071637","stem":"A 56 year old patient with a six year history of peritonitis has died. During dis- section the capsule of the liver and the spleen was markedly thickened in places and was noted as being dense and semi-lucent. The most credible explanation for this is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Hyalinosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Necrosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Mucoid swelling 8"},{"label":"D","text":"Fibrinoid swelling"},{"label":"E","text":"Amyloidosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-173c6c2a49be","stem":"The dissection of a 48 year old patient who suffered with rheumatoid arthritis reveals an enlarged, dense spleen. A spleen‘s section demonstrates its brown- reddish color with enlarged follicles which have the appearance of semi-lucent, grayish-white corns. What is the name of these lesions in the spleen?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Sago-like spleen."},{"label":"B","text":"Glazed spleen."},{"label":"C","text":"Sebaceous spleen."},{"label":"D","text":"Hyalinosis of spleen."},{"label":"E","text":"Porphyry spleen."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b41fe049ff6f","stem":"During the post-mortem performed on a 72 year old man there are noted some diminished areas of the spleen with a pinkish color. Microscopic examination re- vealed that the follicles are diminished in volume and the walls of the arterioles and trabeculas are thickened as well as containing homogeneous eosinophilic, PAS- positive masses. Staining with picrofuksin dye reveals the masses to be a red color. These changes indicate the presence of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Hyalinosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Amyloidosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Mucoid swelling"},{"label":"D","text":"Fibrinoid swelling"},{"label":"E","text":"Sclerosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f12ce431a008","stem":"A 52 year old male died from a heart attack. At the time of dissection a symme- tric type of severe obesity discovered. The rupture of the right ventriculum wall resulted in hemopericardium. Under epicardium an excessive fat tissue formation discovered. A microscopy of the sample showed the excecive growth of fatty tissue accompanied with atrophy of myocardial fibers. Which pathological process is most likely responsible for the patient‘s death?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","sug